  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine Crisis 2022 - WFP Ukraine Limited Emergency Operation 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Aktuellt insats avser Sidas bidrag av medel till WFP med anledning av den f&#xf6;rs&#xe4;mrade livsmedelssituationen och det sv&#xe5;ra tilltr&#xe4;det i Afghanistan, Burkina Faso, Kamerun, Centralafrikanska republiken, Tchad, Demokratiska republiken Kongo, Etiopien, Jemen, Mali, Mo&#xe7;ambique, Myanmar, Niger, Nigeria, Somalia, Sydsudan, Sudan, Uganda och Venezuela.

St&#xf6;det omfattar 348 miljoner kronor f&#xf6;r att n&#xe5; krisdrabbade m&#xe4;nniskor i 18 kontexter under 2022. 274 MSEK (78 %) &#xe4;r &#xe4;mnad f&#xf6;r livsmedelsinsatser i 11 kriser och 74 MSEK (22 %) g&#xe5;r till UNHAS i 11 kontexter. I fyra l&#xe4;nder, DR Kongo, Jemen, Mocambique och Nigeria t&#xe4;cker st&#xf6;det b&#xe5;de livsmedelsassistans och UNHAS.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sida will contribute a total of 348 million SEK to WFP to respond to the humanitarian needs of affected populations during 2022, within two main categories: a) Crisis response through food, nutrition and resilience assistance - 274 MSEK, and b) enhanced access through UN Humanitarian Air Services - 74 MSEK.

This support will be channelled through WFP&apos;s Country Strategic Plans (CSP) in 18 crises: Afghanistan - Crisis Response (50 MSEK), Burkina Faso - UNHAS (4 MSEK), Cameroon - UNHAS (4 MSEK), Central African Republic (CAR) - UNHAS (9 MSEK), Chad - UNHAS (4 MSEK), Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) - Crisis Response (35 MSEK) and UNHAS (10 MSEK), Ethiopia - Crisis Response (65 MSEK), Mali - UNHAS 5 MSEK, Mozambique - Crisis Response (7 MSEK) and UNHAS (3 MSEK), Myanmar - Crisis Response (14 MSEK), Niger - UNHAS (4 MSEK), Nigeria - Crisis Response (20 MSEK) and UNHAS (15 MSEK), Somalia - Crisis Response (13 MSEK), South Sudan - Crisis Response (15 MSEK), Sudan - UNHAS (6 MSEK), Uganda - Crisis Response (20 MSEK), Venezuela - Country Response (10 MSEK), Yemen - Crisis Response (25 MSEK) and UNHAS (10 MSEK).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WFP is Sida&apos;s main partner for responding to food needs in humanitarian settings, and has proven to be a highly effective partner in providing the assistance and protection to the most affected populations. WFP&apos;s capacity has been strengthened through the reform process which the organization underwent during the previous agreement period.

Sida will contribute funds to WFP to respond to the humanitarian needs of affected populations during 2022, within two main categories: a) Crisis response through food, nutrition and resilience assistance  and b) enhanced access through UNHAS.</narrative>
  </description>
